// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHALE FLOW & MACRO v4 — lower-pane companion (separate panel under candles)
//
//  WHAT IT ACTUALLY MEASURES (honest version):
//  TradingView cannot see whale wallets, order books, or exchange long/short
//  account ratios — no Pine script can. This panel uses the best proxies that
//  TV data really provides:
//
//  ① VOLUME DELTA — each chart bar is split into intrabars; up-closing minute
//    volume counts as aggressive buying, down-closing as selling. Columns in
//    % of bar volume (−100…+100). Whale bars (top-percentile volume) bright.
//    WHALE BIAS line = net direction of ONLY the whale bars, rolling window.
//  ② CVD DIVERGENCE — price makes a higher high while cumulative volume delta
//    makes a lower high → the rally isn't backed by real buying (bearish ▼).
//    Mirror for lows (bullish ▲). Markers confirm `pivot length` bars after
//    the pivot — delayed, but they never repaint once shown.
//  ③ OPEN INTEREST READ — the closest thing to "opening long or short",
//    aggregated across venues (avg of each venue's Δ%, so different contract
//    units can't distort the sum) and smoothed:
//       OI ↑ + price ↑  = new LONGS opening        (green strip)
//       OI ↑ + price ↓  = new SHORTS opening       (red strip)
//       OI ↓ + price ↑  = shorts CLOSING (squeeze) (teal strip)
//       OI ↓ + price ↓  = longs CLOSING (flush)    (orange strip)
//    OI alone can't say WHO opened — every long has a short on the other side
//    — which is why it's paired with the delta above.
//  ④ DXY LINK — rolling correlation of RETURNS between this symbol and the US
//    Dollar Index, reported in the table. Crypto/DXY correlation is TYPICALLY
//    inverse but unstable — context, not a rule.
//
// ─── WHAT CHANGED IN v4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  The same four measurements as v3, with 25 inputs cut to 8 and two remaining
//  measurement defects fixed. Nothing was simplified by lowering the standard:
//  every v3 correction is still here, the knobs that encoded them are just no
//  longer the user's problem.
//
//  1. EVERY WINDOW IS A LENGTH OF TIME, NOT A BAR COUNT. v3 shipped a footnote
//     reading "defaults tuned for 15m; on 30m set Percentile Lookback 100, Bias
//     Window 48, Correlation Length 100". That is arithmetic the script can do
//     itself, and a user who skips it silently measures something else — the
//     same "200 bars" is 2 days on 15m and 8 days on 1h. v4 states the windows
//     in hours and derives bar counts from timeframe.in_seconds(), so the panel
//     means the same thing on every timeframe.
//  2. THE INTRABAR TIMEFRAME AUTO-SELECTS. Same story: v3 told the user to
//     switch to "3" on 30m to stretch the covered history. v4 targets ~15
//     slices per chart bar and snaps to a real TV timeframe — which lands on
//     exactly the values v3 recommended by hand.
//  3. OI OUTAGES WERE COUNTED AS "OI DIDN'T MOVE" — a real defect that v3 fixed
//     for the dollar and missed here. v3 smoothed with ta.ema(nz(oiRawDelta),n):
//     when no venue reported, nz() fed a 0 into the EMA. That is a fabricated
//     observation, the identical mistake v3 correctly removed from the DXY
//     correlation where repeated weekend closes were being read as "the dollar
//     was flat". v4 advances the OI average only on bars where a venue actually
//     reported, holds its last value across an outage, and refuses to call a
//     state once the feed has gone stale.
//  4. THE ROLLING CORRELATION COULD DRIFT. Returns are ~1e-4 and their squares
//     ~1e-8, so an O(1) accumulator that adds an entering pair and subtracts a
//     leaving one loses significance over a long history — v3 guarded the
//     symptom (`varX > 0`) rather than the cause. v4 keeps the O(1) update for
//     speed but rebuilds the five sums exactly from the retained window once
//     per window length, so error can never compound.
//  Also: the DXY correlation line left the pane. Correlation×100 shares the
//  −100…100 range with delta% and Whale Bias by coincidence, not because it is
//  the same quantity, so three unrelated meanings were sharing one axis.
//
//  Kept from v3, unchanged: gap-aware DXY return pairing, the true/estimated
//  delta split with hollow markers, ATR-relative significance floors on
//  divergences, venue-agreement reporting, the prior-bar whale percentile, and
//  Whale Bias reading n/a rather than 0 when the window holds no whale bars.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//@version=6
indicator("Whale Flow & Macro", overlay=false, format=format.price, precision=1)

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  INPUTS — eight; everything else is derived            ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
gW = "Flow"
whalePct = input.int(90, "Whale Percentile", minval=70, maxval=99, group=gW, tooltip="A bar is a 'whale bar' when its volume is at or above this percentile of the PRIOR bars. 90 = bigger than 90% of the last two days.")
biasTh   = input.int(40, "Bias Flip Threshold (±)", minval=10, maxval=90, group=gW, tooltip="Whale Bias crossing above +threshold / below −threshold fires the flip alerts and colors the table.")
divMode  = input.string("Normal", "CVD Divergence", ["Off", "Normal", "Strict"], group=gW, tooltip="Compares consecutive price pivots against cumulative volume delta. Higher price high + lower CVD high = bearish ▼ (rally without real buying); mirror for bullish ▲. Markers confirm a few bars after the pivot — no repaint. HOLLOW = at least one pivot came from the estimated delta rather than true intrabar data. Strict widens the pivot window and roughly doubles the significance floors.")

gO = "Open Interest"
oiVenues   = input.string("Binance + Bybit + OKX", "Venues", ["Binance + Bybit + OKX", "Binance + Bybit", "Binance only", "This chart only"], group=gO, tooltip="Each venue contributes its own Δ% (not raw contracts), so different contract units can't distort the average. A venue that doesn't list this coin returns nothing and is skipped; if none report, the chart's own _OI feed is used.")
oiMajority = input.bool(true, "Require Venue Majority", group=gO, tooltip="ON: a state is only called when more than half the venues that moved agree on direction. OFF: the average decides alone, which can print 'Flat' when venues are in fact strongly split — and the split itself is usually worth seeing.")

gD = "Macro"
dxySym = input.symbol("TVC:DXY", "Dollar Index (blank = off)", group=gD, tooltip="Correlation of RETURNS against this symbol, shown in the table. Bars where the dollar market was shut are skipped rather than counted as zero-return, so a weekend cannot drag the reading toward 'no relationship'.")

gP = "Panel"
tblPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Table Position", ["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left", "Hidden"], group=gP)
tblSize = input.string(size.small, "Text Size", [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal], group=gP)

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  DERIVED SETTINGS — windows in time, not in bars       ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) is a SIMPLE int, so everything built
// from it still qualifies as the `simple int` length that ta.* functions need.
// Written inline rather than through a helper on purpose: a user-defined
// function can be inferred as `series`, and a series length is a compile error.
// Floors are sample-size requirements (a percentile over 12 bars is noise);
// ceilings keep a seconds-scale chart from demanding 172,800 bars of history.
tfSec = math.max(60, timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period))

pctLen  = math.min(2000, math.max(50, int(math.round(48.0 * 3600 / tfSec))))  // 2 days
biasLen = math.min(2000, math.max(20, int(math.round(24.0 * 3600 / tfSec))))  // 1 day
corrLen = math.min(1000, math.max(30, int(math.round(48.0 * 3600 / tfSec))))  // 2 dollar-TRADING days

// Intrabar timeframe: target ~15 slices per chart bar — fine enough to classify
// aggression, coarse enough that TV's intrabar history limit doesn't truncate
// the sample early. Snapped to real TV timeframes.
// Boundaries are the GEOMETRIC means between the available timeframes, so each
// chart TF lands on the nearest real one by ratio (60·180 → 104, 180·300 → 232,
// …). Rounding to the next size UP instead would put 4h on 30m = 8 slices when
// 15m gives 16, which is the closer fit.
ltfWant = tfSec / 15
ltfTf   = ltfWant <= 104 ? "1" : ltfWant <= 232 ? "3" : ltfWant <= 520 ? "5" : ltfWant <= 1273 ? "15" : ltfWant <= 2546 ? "30" : "60"

// Divergence presets — one input instead of three.
showDiv   = divMode != "Off"
strict    = divMode == "Strict"
divLen    = strict ? 8 : 5
divMinAtr = strict ? 0.50 : 0.25    // min price-pivot separation, × ATR
divMinCvd = strict ? 0.35 : 0.15    // min CVD-pivot separation, × avg bar delta

// OI smoothing and the flat-tape deadband. These are regime constants, not
// preferences: per-bar OI flips constantly, and a dead tape must not read as
// "longs opening" purely because price changed by +0.00001.
oiSmoothLen = 3
oiDead      = 0.05                  // × ATR
oiMaxStale  = 3                     // bars without an OI print before the read voids

useBinance  = oiVenues != "This chart only"
useBybit    = oiVenues == "Binance + Bybit + OKX" or oiVenues == "Binance + Bybit"
useOkx      = oiVenues == "Binance + Bybit + OKX"

// colors (match the All-in-One palette)
BUY  = #26a69a
SELL = #ef5350
AMBR = #ffb300
TEAL = #4dd0e1
ORNG = #ff9800

atrRef = ta.atr(14)

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  ① VOLUME DELTA + WHALE BARS                           ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// intrabar signed volume: up-closing minute = buy, down-closing = sell
f_delta() =>
    close > open ? volume : close < open ? -volume : close >= nz(close[1], close) ? volume : -volume

deltaArr = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfTf, f_delta())

// Beyond TradingView's intrabar history limit the array comes back empty and
// we fall back to estimating the buy share from where the bar closed inside
// its own range. The two methods do NOT measure the same thing, so which one
// produced a bar is tracked and shown rather than blended silently.
bool  isEst    = deltaArr.size() == 0
float rawDelta = not isEst ? deltaArr.sum() : (high == low ? 0.0 : nz(volume) * (2 * (close - low) / (high - low) - 1))
float deltaPct = nz(volume) > 0 ? rawDelta / volume * 100 : 0.0

// Rank this bar against the bars BEFORE it — a percentile window containing the
// bar itself lets a single huge print raise its own bar for admission. Held
// back until the window is genuinely full, so early bars can't qualify against
// a handful of samples.
whaleThr = ta.percentile_nearest_rank(volume[1], pctLen, whalePct)
isWhale  = bar_index > pctLen and not na(whaleThr) and nz(volume) >= whaleThr

whaleSigned = isWhale ? rawDelta : 0.0
whaleAbs    = isWhale ? math.abs(rawDelta) : 0.0
biasNum     = math.sum(whaleSigned, biasLen)
biasDen     = math.sum(whaleAbs, biasLen)
// na (not 0) when the window holds no whale bars — "we haven't seen size" and
// "size traded and cancelled out" are different statements
float whaleBias = biasDen > 0 ? biasNum / biasDen * 100 : na

var int lastWhaleBar = na
var int lastWhaleDir = 0
if isWhale
    lastWhaleBar := bar_index
    lastWhaleDir := rawDelta >= 0 ? 1 : -1

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  ① b  CVD DIVERGENCE                                   ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
var float cvd = 0.0
cvd += rawDelta
cvdRef = ta.sma(math.abs(rawDelta), 50)      // typical bar delta, for the floor

divPH = ta.pivothigh(high, divLen, divLen)
divPL = ta.pivotlow(low, divLen, divLen)

var float prevPH    = na
var float prevPHcvd = na
var bool  prevPHest = false
var float prevPL    = na
var float prevPLcvd = na
var bool  prevPLest = false

bool bearDiv = false
bool bullDiv = false
bool bearEst = false
bool bullEst = false

// values as they stood AT the pivot, which is divLen bars back at confirmation
float atrAtPivot = nz(atrRef[divLen])
float cvdAtPivot = cvd[divLen]
float refAtPivot = nz(cvdRef[divLen])
bool  estAtPivot = isEst[divLen]

if not na(divPH)
    priceOk = not na(prevPH) and (divPH - prevPH) > atrAtPivot * divMinAtr
    cvdOk   = not na(prevPHcvd) and (prevPHcvd - cvdAtPivot) > refAtPivot * divMinCvd
    if priceOk and cvdOk
        bearDiv := true
        bearEst := estAtPivot or prevPHest
    prevPH    := divPH
    prevPHcvd := cvdAtPivot
    prevPHest := estAtPivot
if not na(divPL)
    priceOkL = not na(prevPL) and (prevPL - divPL) > atrAtPivot * divMinAtr
    cvdOkL   = not na(prevPLcvd) and (cvdAtPivot - prevPLcvd) > refAtPivot * divMinCvd
    if priceOkL and cvdOkL
        bullDiv := true
        bullEst := estAtPivot or prevPLest
    prevPL    := divPL
    prevPLcvd := cvdAtPivot
    prevPLest := estAtPivot

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  ② OPEN INTEREST — aggregated Δ% across venues         ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
f_oiDeltaPct(string tick) =>
    c = request.security(tick, timeframe.period, close, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
    not na(c) and nz(c[1]) > 0 ? (c - c[1]) / c[1] * 100 : na

baseCoin = syminfo.basecurrency
dBin   = f_oiDeltaPct("BINANCE:" + baseCoin + "USDT.P_OI")
dByb   = f_oiDeltaPct("BYBIT:"   + baseCoin + "USDT.P_OI")
dOkx   = f_oiDeltaPct("OKX:"     + baseCoin + "USDT.P_OI")
dChart = f_oiDeltaPct(syminfo.tickerid + "_OI")   // fallback when no venue reports

// each venue contributes (delta, counted?, up?, down?) so the aggregate keeps
// the direction split, not just the average
f_venue(bool on, float d) =>
    ok = on and not na(d)
    [ok ? d : 0.0, ok ? 1 : 0, ok and d > 0 ? 1 : 0, ok and d < 0 ? 1 : 0]

[aD, aC, aP, aN] = f_venue(useBinance, dBin)
[bD, bC, bP, bN] = f_venue(useBybit,   dByb)
[cD, cC, cP, cN] = f_venue(useOkx,     dOkx)
float sumD = aD + bD + cD
int   cntD = aC + bC + cC
int   posD = aP + bP + cP
int   negD = aN + bN + cN

float oiRawDelta = cntD > 0 ? sumD / cntD : dChart
string venueTxt  = cntD > 0 ? str.tostring(cntD) + " ex · " + str.tostring(posD) + "↑" + str.tostring(negD) + "↓" : "chart"
oiOk = not na(oiRawDelta)

// Venue agreement, judged only among venues that actually MOVED. Averaging
// Binance +1.2% with OKX −1.1% yields ≈0 and prints "Flat" — but venues pulling
// in opposite directions is a real, and usually interesting, condition rather
// than a quiet one.
int   dirN     = posD + negD
bool  oiSplit  = dirN > 1 and posD > 0 and negD > 0 and math.max(posD, negD) * 2 <= dirN
bool  oiAgreed = dirN <= 1 or math.max(posD, negD) * 2 > dirN

// Smoothed regime read. The average is advanced ONLY on bars where OI actually
// reported: feeding nz(...)=0 through an outage asserts "open interest did not
// change", a fabricated observation — the same defect that made repeated
// weekend dollar closes read as "the dollar was flat".
var float oiDeltaS  = na
var int   lastOiBar = na
float oiAlpha = 2.0 / (oiSmoothLen + 1)
if oiOk
    oiDeltaS  := na(oiDeltaS) ? oiRawDelta : oiDeltaS + (oiRawDelta - oiDeltaS) * oiAlpha
    lastOiBar := bar_index
int  oiAge   = na(lastOiBar) ? 999999 : bar_index - lastOiBar
bool oiStale = oiAge > oiMaxStale

priceChgS = ta.ema(ta.change(close), oiSmoothLen)
// a dead tape must not read as "up" just because the change was +0.00001
float pDead = nz(atrRef) * oiDead
int   pDir  = priceChgS > pDead ? 1 : priceChgS < -pDead ? -1 : 0

// 1 = longs opening, 2 = shorts opening, 3 = shorts closing, 4 = longs closing
bool oiUsable = not na(oiDeltaS) and not oiStale and (oiAgreed or not oiMajority)
int oiState = not oiUsable or pDir == 0 ? 0 : oiDeltaS > 0 ? (pDir > 0 ? 1 : 2) : oiDeltaS < 0 ? (pDir > 0 ? 3 : 4) : 0
color oiCol = oiState == 1 ? BUY : oiState == 2 ? SELL : oiState == 3 ? TEAL : oiState == 4 ? ORNG : oiSplit ? AMBR : color.new(color.gray, 60)
string oiTxt = oiState == 1 ? "Longs opening" : oiState == 2 ? "Shorts opening" : oiState == 3 ? "Shorts closing" : oiState == 4 ? "Longs closing" : na(oiDeltaS) ? "n/a on this chart" : oiStale ? "no OI print (" + str.tostring(oiAge) + " bars)" : oiSplit ? "Venues split" : "Flat"

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  ③ DXY LINK — correlation over DOLLAR-TRADING bars     ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// gaps_on so a closed dollar market returns na instead of repeating its last
// close. Repeated closes look like "the dollar was flat", which is a fabricated
// observation, and enough of them will drive any correlation toward zero.
useDxy = dxySym != ""
dxyRaw = request.security(useDxy ? dxySym : syminfo.tickerid, timeframe.period, close, gaps=barmerge.gaps_on, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
bool dxyFresh = useDxy and not na(dxyRaw)

var float dxyHeld = na
if dxyFresh
    dxyHeld := dxyRaw
dxyOk = not na(dxyHeld)

// Pair each dollar return with the crypto return over the SAME span, so a
// two-day dollar move is never matched against one 15m candle. Pairs spanning
// a longer market closure than this are dropped entirely.
dxyMaxGap = math.min(500, math.max(4, int(math.round(2.0 * 3600 / tfSec))))
var float prevDxy   = na
var float prevClose = na
var int   prevBar   = na
float rx = na
float ry = na
if dxyFresh
    // a huge sentinel rather than na — it fails the gap test on its own and
    // keeps the expression free of na type-inference surprises
    gap = na(prevBar) ? 999999 : bar_index - prevBar
    if not na(prevDxy) and prevDxy > 0 and not na(prevClose) and prevClose > 0 and gap <= dxyMaxGap
        rx := close / prevClose - 1
        ry := dxyRaw / prevDxy - 1
    prevDxy   := dxyRaw
    prevClose := close
    prevBar   := bar_index

// Rolling Pearson over just the valid pairs. O(1) per bar, but the five sums
// are rebuilt exactly from the window once per window length: returns are ~1e-4
// and their squares ~1e-8, so add-one/subtract-one accumulators lose
// significance over a long history and can even drive the variance negative.
var array<float> cxA = array.new<float>()
var array<float> cyA = array.new<float>()
var float sX  = 0.0
var float sY  = 0.0
var float sXX = 0.0
var float sYY = 0.0
var float sXY = 0.0
var int   sinceExact = 0

if not na(rx) and not na(ry)
    array.push(cxA, rx)
    array.push(cyA, ry)
    sX  += rx
    sY  += ry
    sXX += rx * rx
    sYY += ry * ry
    sXY += rx * ry
    if array.size(cxA) > corrLen
        ox = array.shift(cxA)
        oy = array.shift(cyA)
        sX  -= ox
        sY  -= oy
        sXX -= ox * ox
        sYY -= oy * oy
        sXY -= ox * oy
    sinceExact += 1
    // `for 0 to size-1` counts DOWN when size is 0, so the guard is load-bearing
    if sinceExact >= corrLen and array.size(cxA) > 0
        sinceExact := 0
        sX  := 0.0
        sY  := 0.0
        sXX := 0.0
        sYY := 0.0
        sXY := 0.0
        for i = 0 to array.size(cxA) - 1
            vx = array.get(cxA, i)
            vy = array.get(cyA, i)
            sX  += vx
            sY  += vy
            sXX += vx * vx
            sYY += vy * vy
            sXY += vx * vy

int   nPair  = array.size(cxA)
minN         = math.max(30, corrLen / 4)
float varX   = nPair * sXX - sX * sX
float varY   = nPair * sYY - sY * sY
float denomC = varX > 0 and varY > 0 ? math.sqrt(varX * varY) : 0.0
float corr   = nPair >= minN and denomC > 0 ? (nPair * sXY - sX * sY) / denomC * 100 : na

dxyEma = ta.ema(dxyHeld, math.min(500, math.max(10, int(math.round(12.0 * 3600 / tfSec)))))
dxyUp  = dxyOk and not na(dxyEma) and dxyHeld > dxyEma
// how long since the dollar last printed — the honest way to say "stale"
var int lastDxyBar = na
if dxyFresh
    lastDxyBar := bar_index
dxyAge = na(lastDxyBar) ? 999999 : bar_index - lastDxyBar
bool dxyStale = dxyAge > dxyMaxGap

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  PLOTS — one axis, one meaning: net flow in %          ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
colDelta = isWhale ? (rawDelta >= 0 ? color.new(BUY, 0) : color.new(SELL, 0)) : (rawDelta >= 0 ? color.new(BUY, 72) : color.new(SELL, 72))
plot(deltaPct, "Delta % of Volume", style=plot.style_columns, color=colDelta)

biasCol = na(whaleBias) ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : whaleBias >= biasTh ? color.new(BUY, 0) : whaleBias <= -biasTh ? color.new(SELL, 0) : color.new(color.silver, 20)
plot(whaleBias, "Whale Bias", color=biasCol, linewidth=2)

hline(0, "Zero", color=color.new(color.gray, 60))
hline(40, "", color=color.new(color.gray, 80), linestyle=hline.style_dotted)
hline(-40, "", color=color.new(color.gray, 80), linestyle=hline.style_dotted)

// Shown when a state is called, and ALSO when venues are split — a split is
// suppressed to state 0 by the majority rule, so testing the state alone would
// silently hide the one condition the amber colour exists to report.
plotshape(oiState != 0 or oiSplit, "OI State Strip", shape.square, location.top, color=oiCol, size=size.tiny)
// filled = both pivots measured from true intrabar delta; hollow = at least one
// came from the close-position estimate, so trust it less
plotshape(showDiv and bearDiv and not bearEst, "Bearish CVD Divergence", shape.triangledown, location.bottom, color.new(SELL, 0), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showDiv and bullDiv and not bullEst, "Bullish CVD Divergence", shape.triangleup,   location.bottom, color.new(BUY, 0),  size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showDiv and bearDiv and bearEst, "Bearish CVD Divergence (estimated)", shape.triangledown, location.bottom, color.new(SELL, 55), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showDiv and bullDiv and bullEst, "Bullish CVD Divergence (estimated)", shape.triangleup,   location.bottom, color.new(BUY, 55),  size=size.tiny)

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  SUMMARY TABLE — six rows                              ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
f_pos(p) => p == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : p == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : p == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

var table tbl = table.new(f_pos(tblPos), 2, 6, bgcolor=color.new(#0d0d12, 15), border_color=color.new(color.gray, 65), border_width=1, frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 45), frame_width=1)

if barstate.islast and tblPos != "Hidden"
    // The delta source rides in the header instead of costing a row — it is
    // always visible, and it is the caveat every other number depends on.
    srcTxt = isEst ? "estimated" : ltfTf + "m intrabar"
    srcCol = isEst ? AMBR : color.new(color.silver, 25)

    biasTxt = na(whaleBias) ? "no whale bars" : whaleBias >= biasTh ? "LONG lean" : whaleBias <= -biasTh ? "SHORT lean" : "Neutral"
    biasC   = na(whaleBias) ? color.gray : whaleBias >= biasTh ? BUY : whaleBias <= -biasTh ? SELL : AMBR
    biasVal = na(whaleBias) ? "" : str.tostring(math.round(whaleBias)) + " · "
    whaleAgoTxt = na(lastWhaleBar) ? "—" : str.tostring(bar_index - lastWhaleBar) + " bars ago " + (lastWhaleDir > 0 ? "▲" : "▼")
    whaleAgoCol = na(lastWhaleBar) ? color.gray : lastWhaleDir > 0 ? BUY : SELL
    oiCell  = oiTxt + (na(oiDeltaS) or oiStale ? "" : " · " + venueTxt)
    corrTxt = na(corr) ? "…" : str.tostring(corr, "#")
    dxyTxt  = not dxyOk ? "off" : (dxyUp ? "Rising" : "Falling") + " · corr " + corrTxt + (dxyStale ? " (mkt shut)" : "")
    dxyC    = not dxyOk ? color.gray : dxyStale ? color.new(color.silver, 30) : dxyUp ? SELL : BUY   // rising dollar = usual crypto headwind (tendency, not a rule)
    // transparent tally — which components lean which way, no composite score
    int leanL = (na(whaleBias) ? 0 : whaleBias >= biasTh ? 1 : 0) + (oiState == 1 or oiState == 3 ? 1 : 0)
    int leanS = (na(whaleBias) ? 0 : whaleBias <= -biasTh ? 1 : 0) + (oiState == 2 or oiState == 4 ? 1 : 0)
    leanTxt = leanL == 0 and leanS == 0 ? "no clear lean" : str.tostring(leanL) + " long / " + str.tostring(leanS) + " short"
    leanC   = leanL > leanS ? BUY : leanS > leanL ? SELL : AMBR

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, " WHALE FLOW", text_color=color.white, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(#1c1c28, 0))
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 0, srcTxt + " ", text_color=srcCol, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(#1c1c28, 0))
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 1, " Whale Bias", text_color=color.silver, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 1, biasVal + biasTxt + " ", text_color=biasC, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 2, " Last Whale", text_color=color.silver, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 2, whaleAgoTxt + " ", text_color=whaleAgoCol, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 3, " Open Interest", text_color=color.silver, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 3, oiCell + " ", text_color=oiCol, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 4, " Dollar", text_color=color.silver, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 4, dxyTxt + " ", text_color=dxyC, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 5, " Net read", text_color=color.silver, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 5, leanTxt + " ", text_color=leanC, text_size=tblSize, text_halign=text.align_right)

// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  ALERTS                                                ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// Bias alerts require a real reading on BOTH bars: nz()-ing an empty window to
// 0 would let "no whale bars → whale bars" print as a threshold crossing.
biasLive = not na(whaleBias) and not na(whaleBias[1])
alertcondition(isWhale and rawDelta > 0, "Whale Buy Bar",  "Top-percentile volume bar hit the BUY side")
alertcondition(isWhale and rawDelta < 0, "Whale Sell Bar", "Top-percentile volume bar hit the SELL side")
alertcondition(biasLive and whaleBias > biasTh and whaleBias[1] <= biasTh,   "Whale Bias Flip Long",  "Whale flow bias crossed above the long threshold")
alertcondition(biasLive and whaleBias < -biasTh and whaleBias[1] >= -biasTh, "Whale Bias Flip Short", "Whale flow bias crossed below the short threshold")
alertcondition(oiState == 1 and oiState[1] != 1, "New Longs Opening",  "Aggregated OI rising with price rising — new longs entering")
alertcondition(oiState == 2 and oiState[1] != 2, "New Shorts Opening", "Aggregated OI rising with price falling — new shorts entering")
alertcondition(oiSplit and not oiSplit[1], "OI Venues Split", "Venues disagree on the direction of open interest — localised flow rather than a market-wide move")
alertcondition(bearDiv, "Bearish CVD Divergence", "Higher price high without higher cumulative delta — rally not backed by real buying")
alertcondition(bullDiv, "Bullish CVD Divergence", "Lower price low without lower cumulative delta — selloff not backed by real selling")
